---
// Running a model by hand, without the router: the resolver and the routing
// table, computed by the kit at build time. Machinery, under the docs.
import DocLayout from '../../layouts/DocLayout.astro';
import LaneResolver from '../../components/LaneResolver.astro';
import RoutingTable from '../../components/RoutingTable.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.astro';
import kit from '../../data/kit.json';
import table from '../../data/routing-table.json';

// The legend only earns its place when some role is unsupported.
const anyUnsupported = table.profiles.some((row) => !row.technical_compatibility);
---

<DocLayout
  title="Run a model by hand — delegation-kit"
  description="Without the router: send one task to one model you name, from Claude Code or Codex, and get a receipt."
  path="/docs/dispatch"
>
  <h1>Run a model by hand</h1>

  <p>
    You name the model and its job, and it runs once. Claude Code and Codex can do this for you, but
    only when you ask. Or let your decider propose the model, below.
  </p>
  <p>
    <code>delegation-route resolve --lane &lt;role&gt;</code> lists the models that can take a role (the
    kind of job, such as builder or reviewer) and never runs anything. <code>delegation-run</code> runs
    the one you choose, inside its sandbox, and writes a receipt. A retry or a review is a new run you
    ask for.
  </p>

  <h2>Let the decider propose one</h2>
  <p>
    With a router block in your configuration, the decider can pick the model for a task you are about
    to delegate. It rates the task, keeps only the models in your pool that take the role and that this
    machine can reach, and recommends the cheapest one strong enough, with its reasons. It runs
    nothing: you run the recommendation (PROFILE below), or ask Claude Code or Codex to.
  </p>
  <div class="not-prose">
    <CodeBlock
      label="Terminal"
      code={`delegation-router decide --prompt-file task.md --lane builder --json
delegation-run --profile PROFILE --lane builder \\
  --prompt-file task.md --output result.txt --workdir WORKTREE`}
    />
  </div>
  <p>
    With GLM 5.3 Flash, Kimi K3 and Opus 5.5 among the builders: a rename (rated 0) goes to GLM, the
    cheapest; a concurrency bug rated 2.5 (minimum score 43.6) to Kimi; a task rated 3 to Opus.
  </p>

  <h2>Which models can take a role</h2>
  <p>Pick a role. Computed from kit {kit.version} when the site was built.</p>
  <div class="not-prose">
    <LaneResolver />
  </div>

  <h2>Every role, every model</h2>
  <p>
    {kit.profiles} profiles from the default install. <code>serve</code> does not pick by role;
    <code>decide --lane</code> does, inside your pool.
  </p>
  <div class="not-prose">
    {
      anyUnsupported && (
        <p class="text-[0.75rem] mb-4">
          <span class="status status-unsupported">unsupported</span> the adapter does not support this role;
          never selectable
        </p>
      )
    }
    <RoutingTable />
  </div>

  <p>
    Each CLI runs in its own sandbox with an identity check, and <code>delegation-patch-verify</code> checks
    a text model's patch before you apply it. Details: <a href="/docs/executors/">Executors</a>,
    <a href="/docs/configuration/">Configuration</a>.
  </p>
</DocLayout>
